---
import PirschScript from '@fresh.codes/astro-pirsch-proxy/components/PirschScript.astro'
import config from 'virtual:pirsch-config'

const hitPath = `${config.routePrefix}/${config.endpointNames.hit}`
const sessionPath = `${config.routePrefix}/${config.endpointNames.session}`
---

<html lang='en'>
  <head>
    <meta charset='utf-8' />
    <meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1' />
    <title>Session Tracking Example - Astro Pirsch Proxy</title>
    <PirschScript data-enable-sessions='true' data-interval-ms='10000' />
    <style>
      body {
        font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
        max-width: 800px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 2rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }
      a {
        color: #4338ca;
        text-decoration: none;
      }
      a:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
      }
      .info {
        background: #f3f4f6;
        padding: 1rem;
        border-radius: 0.5rem;
        margin: 1rem 0;
      }
      .success {
        background: #d1fae5;
        border-left: 4px solid #10b981;
      }
      code {
        background: #e5e7eb;
        padding: 0.125rem 0.25rem;
        border-radius: 0.25rem;
        font-size: 0.875rem;
      }
      pre {
        background: #1f2937;
        color: #f3f4f6;
        padding: 1rem;
        border-radius: 0.5rem;
        overflow-x: auto;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <p><a href='/'>← Back to Examples</a></p>

    <h1>Session Tracking Example</h1>

    <div class='info success'>
      <p>
        <strong>Session tracking is enabled!</strong> The Pirsch script will automatically
        send session extension requests every 10 seconds.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class='info'>
      <p>
        <strong>What are sessions?</strong> Sessions track how long visitors stay
        engaged with your site. Unlike page views (which track individual page loads),
        sessions measure continuous engagement.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>How Session Tracking Works</h2>
    <p>Session tracking is configured with two key attributes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>data-enable-sessions="true"</code> - Enables session tracking
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>data-interval-ms="10000"</code> - Sends a session extension every 10
        seconds (10,000ms)
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Script Configuration</h3>
    <pre>&lt;PirschScript
  data-enable-sessions="true"
  data-interval-ms="10000"
/&gt;</pre>

    <div class='info'>
      <h3>Use Cases for Session Tracking</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Engagement:</strong> See how long users actually interact with your
          content
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bounce Rate:</strong> Distinguish between quick visits and engaged
          sessions
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Content Quality:</strong> Measure which pages keep users engaged
          longer
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>User Flow:</strong> Understand how users navigate through your site
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class='info'>
      <h3>Verify in Network Tab</h3>
      <p>Open your browser's developer tools (Network tab) and you'll see:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Initial page hit to <code>{hitPath}</code></li>
        <li>
          Session extensions to <code>{sessionPath}</code> every 10 seconds
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Stay on this page for at least 10 seconds to see the session extensions
        being sent automatically!
      </p>
    </div>

    <p><a href='/'>← Back to Examples</a></p>
  </body>
</html>
